tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-216-c-spelling-carried-into-a-header.hero:14:8: error[unwritable_name]: `<stdio.h>` is C's own `#include` spelling carried into the string, brackets and all, and the `>` would end the name C reads: the group's string holds the name alone, as `extern "stdio.h"`
